        "prompt": "# Kspec Automation Session - Task Work\n\n**Session ID:** `01KJ6NFBHNMBABEHHDVEYSPJFR`\n**Iteration:** 1 of 30\n**Mode:** Automated (no human in the loop)\n\n## Session Focus (applies to ALL iterations)\n\n> **Do your best, ensure code is high quality and you follow all ACs both main specs and attached traits. Be thorough. After submitting a PR run /codex PR and fix any issues it brings up. Ensure when spawning codex that you instruct it that it is running inside of a kspec ralph loop and in no uncertain terms should it blanket kill processes especially kspec or kspec ralph ones. Ensure the code you're writing is tested, reviewed and not only matches the letter of the tasks, specs, and AC but also the spirit. Do better, do more, be proactive and succeed!**\n\nKeep this focus in mind throughout your work. It takes priority over default task selection.\n\n\n## Current State\n```json\n{\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:51:00.325Z\",\n  \"branch\": \"main\",\n  \"context\": {\n    \"focus\": null,\n    \"threads\": [],\n    \"open_questions\": [],\n    \"updated_at\": \"2026-01-22T21:05:45.847Z\"\n  },\n  \"active_tasks\": [],\n  \"pending_review_tasks\": [],\n  \"recent_notes\": [\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJ6M7S\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Fix: detectTaskCompleteCommand should match task submit\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJ6MGF\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:34:07.620Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Fixed two locations:\\n1. detectTaskCompleteCommand() in ralph.ts: regex now matches both 'kspec task complete' and 'kspec task submit' via alternation pattern\\n2. getIterationStats() in session.ts: now counts pending_review tasks (using started_at >= since) in addition to completed tasks (using completed_at >= since)\\nExported detectTaskCompleteCommand for proper unit testing. Updated tests: replaced placeholder expect(true) with real assertions, updated iteration stats test to verify submitted tasks count toward limit. Updated spec ac-detection to reflect submit counting.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJ65H0\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Design native task-limit enforcement for ralph agent iterations\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJ6KNM\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:19:28.013Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Completed with --skip-review: Spike complete. Investigated session scoping approach for kspec, including:\\n- Cross-harness env var research (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI)\\n- Current session/ralph/hook architecture analysis\\n- Design of session-scoped budget enforcement replacing marker files + bash hooks\\n- Dual review (internal + Codex) with all MUST-FIX findings addressed\\n\\nDeliverables:\\n- Plan @plan-session-scoping-for-kspec imported with 6 specs, 10 tasks\\n- Dependencies set between tasks\\n- Specs have traits: @trait-json-output, @trait-semantic-exit-codes, @trait-error-guidance\\n- Key design decisions: budget on local filesystem (not shadow branch), single-writer guarantee, cooperative enforcement, end-loop migrated to session state, sessions always closed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJ65H0\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Design native task-limit enforcement for ralph agent iterations\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJ6JZE\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-24T01:07:21.290Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"## Session Progress \u2014 Spike Investigation Complete, Plan Drafted\\n\\n### What was done\\n1. **Full investigation of session scoping approach** \u2014 explored current session infrastructure, ralph loop, hooks, task schema, and environment variable handling across 4 agent harnesses (Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Gemini CLI).\\n\\n2. **Design decisions made with user:**\\n   - Soft advisory task claiming (not hard isolation)\\n   - Budget enforcement built into kspec task start itself (no hook needed for task limiting)\\n   - Session state machine: ralph unlocks \u2192 agent starts task \u2192 agent submits \u2192 kspec auto-locks \u2192 ralph resets for next iteration\\n   - Single-writer guarantee for atomicity (ralph and agent are never concurrent)\\n   - KSPEC_SESSION_ID env var flows through agent tool calls\\n\\n3. **Plan written in kspec import format** at `/home/chapel/.claude/plans/bright-seeking-marble.md`:\\n   - 5 specs: session-creation-and-env-injection, session-scoped-task-claiming, task-budget-enforcement, native-guard-commands, ralph-session-budget-integration\\n   - 9 tasks covering schema changes, CLI commands, budget enforcement, native guards, ralph simplification, multi-harness env injection\\n   - Dry run passes clean: `kspec plan import --module cli --dry-run`\\n\\n4. **Dual review completed** \u2014 both an internal agent review and Codex review-plan found convergent issues. Reviews saved at `/tmp/codex-plan-review.md`.\\n\\n### Review findings to address before import\\nMUST-FIX:\\n- Add ACs for invalid/stale KSPEC_SESSION_ID (session not found, malformed ID)\\n- Add migration cleanup ACs (remove old hook entries from settings.json, delete old bash scripts)\\n- Add cross-file consistency ACs (task state + budget state divergence on partial failure)\\n- Fix `ac-cleanup` to be concrete and testable\\n\\nSHOULD-FIX (under discussion with user):\\n- Shadow branch contention: should budget state live in local file vs shadow branch?\\n- Submit vs complete with review subagent: should subagent inherit session ID?\\n- End-loop marker: leave as-is or migrate to session state?\\n- Wrap-up message: error message should contain wrap-up instructions\\n- Explicitly state interactive sessions have no budget\\n- Fix file reference: `tasks ready` is in tasks.ts not task.ts\\n- State explicitly that enforcement is cooperative-only\\n\\n### What's left\\n- User wants to discuss specific findings (shadow branch contention, subagent session inheritance, end-loop marker, wrap-up message) before updating the plan\\n- After discussion: update plan with fixes, re-run dry run, import\\n- Then: derive implementation tasks from the plan\\n\\n### Key files\\n- Plan: /home/chapel/.claude/plans/bright-seeking-marble.md\\n- Codex review: /tmp/codex-plan-review.md\\n- Internal review: in conversation context\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJ6CJC\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Clean up obsolete project skills superseded by core skills\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJ6E93\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-23T23:45:15.064Z\",\n      \"author\": \"@claude\",\n      \"content\": \"Completed with --force from in_progress state. Reason: Removed 6 obsolete project skills (create-workflow, reflect, task-work, meta, spec, spec-plan) from .claude/skills/. All content verified covered by core skills. Committed in 91e26c52.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"active_todos\": [],\n  \"ready_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ4SNE\",\n      \"title\": \"task set --spec-ref has no way to clear the field. --plan-ref supports 'null' to clear but --spec-re\",\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ4SNF\",\n      \"title\": \"plan import: add depends_on field to plan YAML spec format so specs/tasks get structural dependencie\",\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"spec_ref\": \"@plan-import\",\n      \"tags\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ4SNG\",\n      \"title\": \"Plan import should support task priority: plan document specs can specify priority, and derived task\",\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"spec_ref\": \"@plan-import\",\n      \"tags\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ4SNH\",\n      \"title\": \"kspec plan import should detect and report YAML-unsafe values in AC fields (colons in then: values) \",\n      \"priority\": 3,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n    