ng. No code changes needed \u2014 existing fallback chains handle everything correctly. Only untested item is permission event fields (low risk, requires non-yolo run).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ4SMA\",\n      \"title\": \"kspec batch cannot handle task patch with nested --data JSON argument. The data object gets stringif\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:38:31.682Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #482. Fixed batch arg serialization to JSON.stringify nested objects instead of String() which produced [object Object]. Added toArgString() helper, comprehensive tests including trait AC coverage, and dry_run boolean field to BatchExecResult.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ65J2\",\n      \"title\": \"Fix phased tool call event handling for ralph display and session stats\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:37:01.844Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"PR #485 merged by @chapel. Fix handles phased tool call events from ACP SDK 0.14+: translator extracts summary from tool_call_update, stats deduplicate by toolCallId, session display filters phased duplicates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ5WV0\",\n      \"title\": \"Fix ralph event logging iteration capture-by-value bug\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T21:36:33.124Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #485. Handles phased tool call events from ACP SDK 0.14+: translator emits summaries when rawInput arrives late, deduplication in session display/stats/search. 7 new tests, all CI green.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ4SMB\",\n      \"title\": \"Bug: `kspec plan import` ignores spec_ref on manual tasks. AC @plan-import ac-27 says manual tasks g\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T18:35:59.940Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #483. Honors spec_ref on manual tasks in plan import. All CI green, audit confirmed clean.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJ4SM9\",\n      \"title\": \"task complete --force should bypass the submit requirement. Currently --force does not skip the in_p\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-23T16:24:01.884Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #481. --force flag now bypasses all state checks in task complete, enabling direct completion from in_progress, pending, blocked, and cancelled states. Documents prior state in note and warning. 7 tests cover all force-complete paths. Spec @task-commands ac-1 fully covered.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recent_commits\": [\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"f9d068a\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"f9d068a0103643543a19e5edabdcced2af9b6ec2\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T01:49:51.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: count task submit toward max-tasks limit (#489)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"0045027\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"004502786bd58e525234b6fcbc04342e7652205f\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T01:42:30.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: use submitted_at timestamp for pending_review iteration counting\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"c3b690f\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"c3b690f14da4521f024197aaa14e81484d839397\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-24T01:34:29.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: count task submit toward max-tasks limit\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"9e47f95\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"9e47f9569fafe7a69e5239e9fe836f6c096137a3\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-23T23:53:25.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"chore: remove 6 obsolete project skills superseded by core skills (#488)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"91e26c5\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"91e26c525b45614dffc86229ecc0f269764bf8f5\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-23T23:45:05.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"chore: remove 6 obsolete project skills superseded by core skills\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"eeac88d\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"eeac88d921e1b8475ecb5e46acd739d25056c39a\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-23T23:24:01.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"chore: bump version to 0.4.0 (#487)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"3da0776\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"3da07761daeb6fa3c75a43d6880f4b7cced4aaea\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-23T23:16:57.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"chore: bump version to 0.4.0\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"764f40d\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"764f40d76b1d519e37086d672ec84fbb103bf377\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-23T23:02:02.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"feat: use index-based iteration boundaries in computeIterationSummaries (#486)\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"93b8931\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"93b8931ebbb3f80eca93dedd03403686940014d5\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-23T22:55:15.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: update stats test for boundary-aware iteration counting\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"775d234\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"775d23415c67e247bb9d36dd08f349279f1160dd\",\n      \"date\": \"2026-02-23T22:47:11.000Z\",\n      \"message\": \"fix: align empty session iteration_count between summary and detail\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"working_tree\": {\n    \"clean\": true,\n    \"staged\": [],\n    \"unstaged\": [],\n    \"untracked\": []\n  },\n  \"inbox_items\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFH76C\",\n      \"text\": \"Cross-feature requirement pattern: How to express that core features (search, validate, export) must support all entity types. When new entity type added, should automatically imply tasks for core features. Options: (1) applies_to field on feature specs, (2) trait on entity types like @trait-searchable, (3) validation warning for missing coverage, (4) parent spec that entity types must satisfy. Surfaced when realizing search doesn't cover inbox.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-21T21:25:59.163Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"design\",\n        \"spec-model\",\n        \"meta\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFHJNZ\",\n      \"text\": \"Reverse spec lookup - kspec which <file> or kspec which <file:line> to find specs/ACs that reference or are implemented by a given code path. Useful for bug fixes to quickly discover what specs need updating. Could scan for // AC: annotations and spec_ref links. Instructive, helps find already-instrumented code.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-22T00:46:44.345Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"dx\",\n        \"tooling\",\n        \"reflection\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFPDCY\",\n      \"text\": \"Add cross-platform CI matrix testing - run core functionality tests on Windows, macOS, and Linux. Would catch issues like Unix-specific commands (which, cp -r) before they reach PR review. Consider: matrix strategy in GitHub Actions, platform-specific test skips where needed, focus on CLI commands and daemon lifecycle.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-23T21:50:37.263Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"ci\",\n        \"testing\",\n        \"dx\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFQ517\",\n      \"text\": \"E2E tests: Use isolated port range (not 3456) + cross-platform cleanup. Current approach conflicts with existing daemons. Should use high ephemeral port range and improve cleanup mechanism.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-24T04:43:39.058Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"e2e\",\n        \"testing\",\n        \"reflection\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KFYAHF\",\n      \"text\": \"E2E test dev mode - configure Playwright to work with vite dev server instead of requiring full build for faster test iteration (12+ seconds to 1-2 seconds)\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-01-26T23:34:35.746Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"e2e\",\n        \"dx\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGG6GY\",\n      \"text\": \"Improve derive granularity: Research suggests specs with 4+ ACs are candidates for splitting. Potential enhancements: (1) --by-ac flag to create tasks per AC group, (2) --max-acs N to auto-group, (3) implementation_phases field in specs, (4) derive templates for common patterns (cli-command, api-endpoint), (5) complexity warnings when specs are too large. See session research on task decomposition patterns from Linear, Atlassian, BDD/Example Mapping, and AI coding assistants.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-02T22:10:44.331Z\",\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGGEMM\",\n      \"text\": \"Daemon debugging improvements: (1) Add --log-file or --verbose to 'kspec serve start', (2) Log resolved web UI path on startup, (3) Capture and show stderr when daemon fails to start within timeout. Consolidated from @01KFQ586, @01KFQ595, @01KFPH3D.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-03T00:32:32.926Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"daemon\",\n        \"dx\",\n        \"deferred\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGGF4Y\",\n      \"text\": \"Project config file (kspec.config.yaml or .kspecrc): Configure shadow remote URL (enable separate repo for specs), feature toggles, default values (author, priority), validation strictness. Enables multi-repo projects sharing specs and tailoring kspec to project needs. Consolidated from @01KFGVVJ, @01KFGVVN.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-03T00:41:28.272Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"feature\",\n        \"config\",\n        \"dx\",\n        \"deferred\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGGFB2\",\n      \"text\": \"AC test coverage analysis: 'kspec coverage @spec-ref' command to scan codebase for '// AC: @spec ac-N' annotations and report which ACs have test coverage vs gaps. Soft check for review, not blocking. Consolidated from @01KFHJNR, @01KFP9A6.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-03T00:44:48.658Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"cli\",\n        \"testing\",\n        \"dx\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KGGG0K\",\n      \"text\": \"Shadow sync improvements: (1) Auto-resolve using rebase/merge-driver for cleaner sync, (2) Make sync warnings visible in CLI output (currently silent unless KSPEC_DEBUG=1), (3) Auto-detect common issues with suggested fixes. Consolidated from @01KFTDA7, @01KFHZR4.\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-02-03T00:56:34.557Z\",\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"shadow\",\n        \"dx\",\n        \"cli\"\n      ],\n      \"added_by\": \"@claude\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"stats\": {\n    \"total_tasks\": 629,\n    \"in_progress\": 0,\n    \"needs_work\": 0,\n    \"pending_review\": 0,\n    \"ready\": 31,\n    \"blocked\": 0,\n    \"completed\": 573,\n    \"inbox_items\": 83\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Instructions\n\nRun the task-work skill in loop mode:\n\n```\n/kspec:task-work loop\n```\n\nLoop mode means: no confirmations, auto-resolve decisions, automation-eligible tasks only.\n\n**Normal flow:** Work on a task, create a PR, then stop responding. Ralph continues automatically \u2014\nit checks for remaining eligible tasks at the start of each iteration and exits the loop itself when none remain.\n\n**Do NOT call `end-loop` after completing a task.** Simply stop responding.\n`end-loop` is a rare escape hatch for when work is stalling across multiple iterations with no progress \u2014 not a normal exit path.\n",
